---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Container from "@/components/container.astro";
import Sectionhead from "@/components/sectionhead.astro";
import ContactCards from "@/components/contact-cards.astro";
import { Icon } from "astro-icon/components";

const founders = [
  {
    name: "Marcin Mazurek",
    role: "Co-founder",
    photo: "/marcin.png",
    linkedin: "#",
    bio: "Has led engineering at scale, building platforms used by millions, where reliability, performance, and business impact are inseparable.",
  },
  {
    name: "Darek Dwornikowski",
    role: "Co-founder",
    photo: "/darek.jpg",
    linkedin: "#",
    bio: "Has been deep in the architecture designing systems that need to work under pressure, across complex environments, with no room for failure.",
  },
];
---

<Layout title="About — Bitropy">
  <Container>
    <Sectionhead>
      <Fragment slot="title">Why we built Bitropy</Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="desc">The enterprise layer for LLM and MCP traffic, built by people who have operated AI in regulated environments.</Fragment>
    </Sectionhead>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl mt-12 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
      <p>
        Bitropy is the missing control layer for AI in the enterprise.
      </p>
      <p>
        Gain full visibility into AI usage across teams, models and data and enforce security, cost and compliance in real time.
      </p>
      <p class="font-medium text-slate-800">
        One endpoint. Full control. No rewrite required.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl mt-20">
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Founders</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
        <p>
          Bitropy is built by people who have spent years building and running large-scale systems where technology decisions don't stay in code, but shape how entire organisations operate.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mt-10">
        {founders.map((f) => (
          <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-6">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
              <img src={f.photo} alt={f.name} class="w-16 h-16 rounded-full object-cover shrink-0 border border-slate-200" />
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-slate-900">{f.name}</h3>
                <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mt-0.5">
                  <p class="text-sm text-[#967deb] font-semibold">{f.role}</p>
                  <a href={f.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-slate-400 hover:text-[#0a66c2] transition" aria-label={`${f.name} on LinkedIn`}>
                    <Icon class="w-4 h-4" name="uil:linkedin" />
                  </a>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="text-slate-600 mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">{f.bio}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
        <p>
          Together, they've seen what happens when new technology outpaces control: systems grow faster than the structure around them, ownership disappears across teams, and costs, risk, and complexity accumulate quietly until they become a problem.
        </p>
        <p class="font-medium text-slate-800">
          AI is repeating the same pattern. Just faster.
        </p>
        <p>
          Bitropy is their response to that — not built from theory, but from experience of what actually breaks at scale and how to fix it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <ContactCards />
  </Container>
</Layout>
